# TUI-DESIGN-2 §8.3 S6: a zero-argument `jevcode` against live Jev through the OpenRouter decisions router (JEV_PROVIDER=openrouter;
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY from the repository's ./.env serves Jev and the generator), the generator key unset in the environment
# (`env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), a temp JEVCODE_HOME, the workspace a fresh copy of examples/demo-py (git init, .venv with
# pytest). Reviews are answered by the driver (PTY_AUTO_REVIEW=y: a one-second look, `y`, then the `confirm <id> approved` line).
# Every pause is a draining `sleep` (research 20 §5).
# 1. the first frame is splash frame 0 (§5.2: the `step 0/–` sentinel, the console and the badge in the same frame); raw mode on;
#    the round-2 placeholder; the session meter arrives after resolveConfig (§5.3)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
mark first-frame
expect step 0/
expect \x1b\[\?2004h
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
mark composer-ready
# 2. no key: the splash settles by itself into the brand row (§5.2 row 14, §5.4)
expect ◆ jevcode
mark splash-settled
sleep 0.3
# 3. a greeting: one Jev intake request, a [you] bubble, a [jevcode] catalogue reply, no run (§3.1 row 6); the wall time
#    hi-sent → hi-reply is the round-2 gate (§9: p95 < 1.5 s live)
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
mark hi-reply
sleep 0.5
# 4. a question about the tool: the harness facts, one [jevcode] item per selected fact (§3.1 row 7, §3.5)
send what can you do?
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark facts-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*what can you do\?
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
mark facts-reply
sleep 0.5
# 5. /jev before any run: `<provider> · <host> · <model> (pinned)` (§2.6 line 1) and the intake line for the two messages
send /jev
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect openrouter · openrouter\.ai · typesafe/jev-1\.13-20260917 \(pinned\)
expect intake: 2 messages
mark jev-before-run
sleep 0.3
# 6. /mode jev-on (§1.3): a generator key resolves from the repository .env (OPENROUTER_API_KEY serves the default
#    `openrouter` generator), so the mode pends for the next run and the badge reads `jev+llm · next run` (§1.5, H-G1);
#    with no generator key the wizard's provider step would open in place instead (`Pick the provider`) — the
#    alternation records which branch ran
send /mode jev-on
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect (jev\+llm from the next run|Pick the provider)
mark mode-jev-on
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*jev\+llm(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* · next run
sleep 0.3
# 7. back to jev-only, so the task below runs with zero generator calls (§1.1)
send /mode jev-only
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect mode jev-only from the next run
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*jev-only(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
mark mode-jev-only
sleep 0.3
# 8. a real task: the intake reads `coding_task` at p ≥ 0.6 → a jev-only run (§3.1 row 5, §3.3 run floor); the compact
#    transcript shows [run] start, one [step N] summary line per step and [run] end (§4.5)
send Fix the failing tests in tests/test_core.py without changing the tests.
sleep 0.3
send \r
mark task-sent
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* start 
mark run-started
expect \[step 1\]
mark step-1
expect end (complete|max_steps|spend_cap|wall_time|human_pause|replan_stop|impossible|error)
mark run-ended
sleep 0.5
# 9. /jev after the run: the served model — the dated id is served verbatim on OpenRouter (§2.5); /cost's chat line (§3.9)
send /jev
sleep 0.2
send \r
#    at 80 columns the detail row wraps after `→ resolved `, so the served id is expected on the continuation row
expect → resolved
expect typesafe/jev-1\.13-20260917
mark jev-after-run
send /cost
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect chat \$
mark cost-shown
sleep 0.3
# 10. leave (exit 0)
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
